<title>USA: U.S. March retail sales rose 0.2 percent.</title>
<headline>U.S. March retail sales rose 0.2 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce Department seasonally adjusted data on U.S. retail sales.</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:   Mar    Feb-(Prev)  Mar97/96</p>
<p> Retail Sales	    0.2    1.5   0.8     5.7</p>
<p> Excluding Autos	 0.5    0.9   0.5     6.0</p>
<p> Auto Sales	     -0.6    3.3   1.7     4.9</p>
<p> Durable Goods	   0.1    3.1   1.6     6.4</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods	0.3    0.4   0.2     5.3</p>
<p> Furniture Stores	0.2    3.4   0.3     4.5</p>
<p> Building Materials    1.6    2.2   2.2    12.3</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:  Mar     Feb-(Previous)    Jan--(Prev)</p>
<p> Retail Sales	 215.57   215.14  213.18   211.96  211.46</p>
<p> Excluding Autos    162.01   161.25  160.18   159.79  159.36</p>
<p> Auto Sales	    53.56    53.89   52.99    52.17   52.10</p>
<p> Durable Goods	 89.28    89.23   87.60    86.52   87.18</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods   126.29   125.91  125.58   125.44  125.28</p>
<p> Furniture Stores    11.93    11.90   11.47    11.52   11.43</p>
<p> Building Materials  11.86    11.67   11.58    11.42   11.33</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:   Mar    Feb-(Prev)  Mar97/96</p>
<p> General Merch.Stores  0.3    1.3   1.8     8.6</p>
<p> Department Stores     0.7    1.5   2.1    10.1</p>
<p> Food Stores	     0.5    0.1  -0.2     3.6</p>
<p> Grocery Stores	  0.7    UNCH -0.1     3.3</p>
<p> Gas Stations	   -0.8   -1.1  -0.2     3.1</p>
<p> Apparel Stores	  0.6    0.3   0.4     5.2</p>
<p> Eat/Drink Places     -0.1   -0.1  -0.6     3.4</p>
<p> Drug Stores	     0.8    1.6   0.6     9.6</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:  Mar     Feb-(Previous)     Jan---(Prev)</p>
<p> Gen.Merch.Stores    27.49    27.41    27.49     27.06   27.02</p>
<p> Department Stores   21.64    21.50    21.60     21.17   21.17</p>
<p> Food Stores	   36.17    35.97    35.91     35.93   35.99</p>
<p> Grocery Stores	34.16    33.94    33.95     33.95   33.98</p>
<p> Gas Stations	  13.39    13.50    13.70     13.65   13.73</p>
<p> Apparel Stores	 9.73     9.67     9.63	9.64    9.59</p>
<p> Eat/Drink Places    20.47    20.49    20.22     20.51   20.34</p>
<p> Drug Stores	    8.02     7.95     7.86	7.83    7.81</p>
<p>Wall Street economists expected March retail sales to rise 0.6 percent, and sales excluding autos to be up 0.4 percent.</p>
<p>The department revised January retail sales to a 1.7 percent increase from a 1.5 percent rise. It revised January sales excluding autos to a 1.6 percent rise from a 1.4 percent increase, and January auto sales to up 2.1 percent from a 1.9 percent rise.</p>
